PRIVATE REFLECTION: {Verb consistently byti/бꙑти "to be" (suppletive). All supplied forms match attested OCS paradigm exactly. Standard imperative on бѫд- stem: 2/3sg бѫди, 3pl бѫдѫ (distinct from 3sg future бѫдєть). 

Round 1 strengthened majority (now 1,3,4,6,7,10-12,15-18) for бѫдѫ as 3pl imperative, reading label as shorthand/typo for distinct plural slot (non-redundant, parallels 1sg future overlap but explicitly imperative). Minority (2,5,8,9,13) still favor бѫдєть via future-stem reuse for hortative/plural; one (14) argues single бѫди covers 3sg/pl by identity with 2sg. 

Key evidence: attested endings (-и sg vs -ѫ pl), no morphology disputes, only label interpretation. Persistent question: one form vs both 3sg/3pl. Evidence continues to favor бѫдѫ as clean completion.}

